Reject a cyclic pairlist chain in RestoreToEnv(), so the load target
stops timing out on pre-1.0 save files whose CDR points back into the
chain.

The pre-1.0 formats (magic 1971/1972) store every pointer as a node offset,
so a CDR can name its own node or an earlier one.  RestoreToEnv()
(src/main/saveload.c) checks each node of the loaded chain since PR#19238
but walks it until R_NilValue, which a cycle never reaches; a tag of
R_MissingArg (offset -4) is a symbol and passes the check.  Detect the
cycle with a second pointer that moves at half the speed (oss-fuzz
testcase 6565685504049152: a 56-byte input with one self-referencing node).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #549 (no Bugzilla report yet).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/main/saveload.c
+++ b/src/main/saveload.c
@@ -2100,7 +2100,7 @@ attribute_hidden SEXP do_save(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP env)
 
 static SEXP RestoreToEnv(SEXP ans, SEXP aenv)
 {
-    SEXP a, names, obj;
+    SEXP a, slow, names, obj;
     int cnt = 0;
     /* Store the components of the list in aenv.  We either replace
      * the existing objects in aenv or establish new bindings for
@@ -2131,13 +2131,20 @@ static SEXP RestoreToEnv(SEXP ans, SEXP aenv)
 	error(_("loaded data is not in pair list form"));
 
     PROTECT(ans);
-    a = ans;
+    a = slow = ans;
     while (a != R_NilValue) {
 	/* a hand-crafted file can splice any object into the chain */
 	if (TYPEOF(a) != LISTSXP || TYPEOF(TAG(a)) != SYMSXP)
 	    error(_("loaded data is not in pair list form"));
 	a = CDR(a);
 	cnt++;
+	/* and the pre-1.0 formats can point a CDR back into the chain:
+	   'slow' follows at half the speed, so a cycle makes them meet */
+	if (cnt % 2 == 0) {
+	    slow = CDR(slow);
+	    if (a == slow)
+		error(_("loaded data is not in pair list form"));
+	}
     }
     PROTECT(names = allocVector(STRSXP, cnt));
     cnt = 0;
